# Reference trees carrying a MANIFEST.tsv are content-hashed by
# harness/_ref_manifest.py, so the bytes on disk have to be the bytes that
# were hashed — on every platform.  Git for Windows checks text files out
# as CRLF by default, which rewrites every .tsv and .xml under these roots
# and makes the integrity gate report a hash mismatch for all 306 files of
# a tree that is in fact pristine.  That is issue #63's failure mode by a
# different route: the harness refusing to run over something that is not
# reference drift.
#
# `-text` rather than `text eol=lf` on purpose.  eol=lf would normalise on
# the way in as well, so a reference regenerated on Windows (Python text
# mode writes CRLF) would be committed as something other than what its
# author hashed, and the manifest would fault on the next fresh checkout.
# `-text` keeps whatever bytes were generated, identical for everyone.
tests/reference/**                          -text
tests/models/feature_coverage/reference/**  -text
